Source: secubox-network-anomaly
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: secubox-network-anomaly
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.0.0)
Recommends: dnsmasq
Description: SecuBox Network Anomaly — DNS-log anomaly detection
 Reads /var/log/dnsmasq.log and flags lookups that deviate from
 baseline patterns (volume, novelty, NXDOMAIN bursts, suspicious
 TLDs).
 .
 Distinct from sibling packages in the threats cluster:
  - secubox-threats — umbrella dashboard (Suricata + WAF
    alerts).
  - secubox-threat-analyst — AI agent that writes detection scenarios.
  - secubox-cve-triage — CVE vulnerability triage.
  - secubox-cyberfeed — threat-intel feed aggregator.
  - secubox-ipblock — nftables-driven IP blocklist enforcement.
  - secubox-openclaw — OSINT / reconnaissance.
 .
 For DNS-layer blocking (rather than detection only), see
 secubox-dns-guard or secubox-vortex-dns.
